[# docs-src/repos/cx-core-code.cxd — the language's page, repo-cx-core-code.html
   (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 2). Facts from the registries;
   the one example from the repository's own corpus (its code suite). #]

[repo name=cx-core-code
  [intro
    """Ring 1 adds execution and nothing else. `cx-core-code` is
       the evaluator, CXPath, the directive set, the bundled standard library
       below, the formatter, the linter and the language server. It adds no
       servers, no protocol stacks and no databases: a Ring-1 program still
       cannot open a socket, and it reads nothing until you grant it
       ([[capabilities]])."""]
  [body
    """The language is the data format with directives: a program is a
       document whose `[?…]` elements the evaluator runs, a query is a
       pattern over the document you already have ([[code]]), and every
       error is a value you match on rather than an exception you catch.
       Effects are deny-by-default; a refusal names the flag that would allow
       the effect and is an ordinary value like any other."""]
  [body
    """It ships `libcx`, the embeddable evaluator the bindings load, and the
       `cli` and `embed` builds of `cx`: the same binary as the platform
       build with the servers left out, so a script or an embedded evaluator
       carries only the two rings. The specification behind every directive
       is projected into one table on the [directive reference](directives.html);
       if a directive is not in that table, it does not exist."""]
  [gives
    """Every Ring 1 module a program can import without leaving the two rings.
       Each row below is a `registry/modules.cxd` row read when this page was
       built, and each links to the reference page the guide projects from
       that module's own documentation — the same source the conformance
       corpus grades."""]
  [try
    """A query grouped by an attribute: every `user` by department, counted.
       There is no object model to build first and no parser to call — the
       program reads the data in the form you wrote it."""]
  [fixture id=program-for-004-group-count]
  [status
    """The language repository builds on the data core alone and is built on
       by the platform's storage engine; the front door compiles its
       evaluator and its bundled modules from the pin, and the `cx` this
       site's examples were replayed against is that build."""]]
